@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/courier#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sosa: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<> a orexis:OntologyGraph ;    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is
    owl:imports <shapes.ttl> .    # the ACTIONS a world imports itself, actions.ttl or actions.answered.ttl, and the answered drive's document brings the rules (#1002)

#  THE COURIER GRID, A DOMAIN.
#  The courier's words, shared by every world that poses a delivery: a cell, its coordinates and which cells are adjacent,
#  a van, a parcel and where it is owed, a driver - a role an agent plays over the vans it drives - and which van it is aboard, where each stands and
#  what an action is filled with, and since #1002 the column and the row a position fix observes. Beside this document the domain ships what delivered means and how far it is
#  (shapes.ttl), which this document imports; its three actions in two documents it does NOT import, a
#  world importing the one it poses — actions.ttl with the drive fictive, actions.answered.ttl with it
#  a command to the van the world answers (#1002); and the driver's boarding (driver.ttl), which a
#  world with a driver imports beside this one, and a world without one never loads. The cells, the vans and the
#  parcels are a world's, since how big the grid is IS the puzzle; where they stand is a world's
#  state. It is the smallest domain whose search NEEDS guiding — a van two cells from a parcel is
#  closer than one five cells away, in the unit a drive costs — and the one whose effects DELETE.

#################  The grid  #################

:Cell a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Cell" ;
    rdfs:comment "A place on the grid, authored by a world with its coordinates. How big the grid is IS the puzzle, so the cells are the world's." .

:x a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain :Cell ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ; rdfs:label "column" .
:y a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain :Cell ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ; rdfs:label "row" ;
    rdfs:comment "Coordinates, which the estimate measures a distance in, and which a fix and a contact report a position in. Which cells a drive can take a van between is `adjacentTo`, never worked out from them by a text of the search." .

:adjacentTo a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain :Cell ; rdfs:range :Cell ; rdfs:label "adjacent to" ;
    rdfs:comment """The one edge a drive takes a van along: from a cell to one adjacent to it, stated each way. A road
    states its edges itself, segment to segment and lane to passing place, since nothing can compute where a
    road goes; a grid is a road where every neighbour is an edge, and its edges are derived at onboarding
    from the coordinates, |dx| + |dy| = 1, into the world's `grid.derived.ttl`, never written by hand
    (knowledge/domain/courier/adjacency.md, navigation-is-a-body-a-mover-and-a-move §4, #1004).""" .

#################  Instruments  #################

:Column a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf sosa:ObservableProperty ; rdfs:label "Column" ;
    rdfs:comment """The column a van stands in, as an instrument observes it: a `sosa:Sensor` hosted by the van and
    observing this property is half its position fix, reporting the van's `courier:x`, and the courier's
    transitions (rules.ttl) conclude the coordinate and then the cell of it. An instrument gives numbers, so
    a position is the two coordinates the cells are authored in, and a cell is found by them (#1002).""" .

:Row a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf sosa:ObservableProperty ; rdfs:label "Row" ;
    rdfs:comment "The row a van stands in, as an instrument observes it: the other half of a position fix, reporting the van's `courier:y`." .

:RelativeColumn a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf sosa:ObservableProperty ; rdfs:label "Relative column" ;
    rdfs:comment """The column of a CONTACT as seen from the van that carries it: a `sosa:Sample` hosted by the van, standing
    for a peer van it `isSampleOf` - a receiver, one per known van - or for nothing named - a radar's slot, an
    obstacle. Two sensors hosted by the contact observe this and `RelativeRow`, each reporting the contact's
    offset from the carrying van, and the courier's transitions add the van's own held coordinates to it and
    find the cell; a vector landing on no cell is a contact beyond range, believed nowhere
    (knowledge/domain/courier/contact.md, #1003).""" .

:RelativeRow a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf sosa:ObservableProperty ; rdfs:label "Relative row" ;
    rdfs:comment "The row of a contact as seen from the van that carries it: the other half of a contact's vector." .

:Obstacle a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Obstacle" ;
    rdfs:comment """A thing a radar sees and nothing identifies: a contact slot standing for nothing named, at the cell its
    vector lands on while something is in range and nowhere otherwise. A van never stands where one is, which a
    world states as a constraint; there is nothing to ask an obstacle (knowledge/domain/courier/obstacle.md).""" .

:Van a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Van" ;
    rdfs:comment "What moves and what carries. A pure subject of the search, with no capability and no grant." .

:Parcel a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Parcel" ;
    rdfs:comment "A thing with somewhere to be." .

:destination a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain :Parcel ; rdfs:range :Cell ; rdfs:label "destination" ;
    rdfs:comment "Where a parcel is owed. Authored and never moved: the world states it, no effect touches it, and it is what the desire's met-test compares against." .

:Driver a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Role ; rdfs:label "Driver" ;
    rdfs:comment """Someone a van needs aboard to move: a ROLE an agent plays, `orexis:plays`, stated by the world in the
    document every agent is given, since a peer finds the agent to ask as the one that plays the driver aboard
    the van in range (#923). The role carries what it is over, the vans it `drives`, as an observer carries its
    sensors; it loads no package, what the agent runs being its self graph's word. A world that names no driver
    moves its vans by the agent's own hand, two at once if it likes, as the dispatcher's do; a world that names
    one has made 'one van at a time' a fact about where the driver is, which every plan respects by construction
    (#903). A drive, a pick or a drop of a van somebody drives, and a boarding, are admitted only through a driver
    the agent plays, so of two agents in one world neither's search moves the other's van (#929, #1002,
    knowledge/domain/courier/driver.md).""" .

:drives a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain :Driver ; rdfs:range :Van ; rdfs:label "drives" ;
    rdfs:comment "The vans a driver may drive and board: the role's context, authored and never moved, as a destination is. The world says which vans need a driver and whose they are in one word, and a van no driver drives moves as before." .

#################  What is true while the world runs  #################

:at a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range :Cell ; rdfs:label "at" ;
    rdfs:comment "Where a van or an unloaded parcel stands. Runtime state, posed in state.ttl: one for a van, and none for a parcel being carried, which is the point — a pick removes it and puts nothing in its place." .

:carriedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain :Parcel ; rdfs:range :Van ; rdfs:label "carried by" ;
    rdfs:comment "The other half of the deletion: a parcel is at a cell or aboard a van, never both and never neither." .

:aboard a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain :Driver ; rdfs:range :Van ; rdfs:label "aboard" ;
    rdfs:comment "The van a driver is in. Runtime state, posed in state.ttl and rewritten by a boarding: one van, since a boarding takes away the van the driver leaves, which is what makes a driver one body in one place. A drive moves the van and the driver with it, so where a driver is aboard is all a drive needs to read." .

#################  What an action is filled with  #################

:van a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain orexis:Action ; rdfs:label "van" ;
    rdfs:comment "The van a drive moves and a pick loads into." .
:parcel a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain orexis:Action ; rdfs:label "parcel" ;
    rdfs:comment "The parcel a pick loads or a drop sets down." .
:to a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain orexis:Action ; rdfs:label "to" ;
    rdfs:comment "Where a drive drives or a drop drops: a cell of the grid." .
:driver a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain orexis:Action ; rdfs:label "driver" ;
    rdfs:comment "The driver a boarding moves into a van." .
